Design: I propose replacing the DenseNet121 backbone with a pretrained EfficientNet-B0 to leverage its more efficient architecture and stronger inductive biases, which often yield higher accuracy on image tasks. We will adapt the classifier head to output a single logit, keep the focal loss and horizontal‐flip TTA unchanged, and train for five epochs to allow the new backbone to converge. This single change should boost the AUROC without altering data pipelines or loss functions.
